  "design": {
    "decision": "Bid high, then play for runs: each consecutive win is worth the size of the contract, so both the bid and the order of play matter.",
    "opponent": "Revealed on the first consecutive win; opponents interrupt runs and defend hard against the big contract.",
    "rationale": "Combines the two strongest common shapes (cb-consecutive-mult and cb-contract-mult) under one condition, scaled by the contract for bid tension; it keeps one trigger and one effect, and the scaling uses the existing per-contract-trick template.",
